# WorkforceOS workflows

Follow `docs/workflows/SERVICE_WORKFLOWS.md` and `docs/requirements/REQUIREMENTS_REGISTRY.md`.

- Support the five launch services only as documented: Professional Search, Military Talent Opportunity Assessment, TA Performance Assessment, Fractional Talent Partner, Workforce Pipeline Assessment.
- Service workflows are version-controlled database records. Agents must query an approved workflow rather than hardcode material process rules.
- Do not improvise material workflow, matching, or military-mapping rules in prompts or agent code.
- New jobs search the internal Talent Network before external sourcing.
- Material AI recommendations need provenance. Material client-facing AI outputs need human approval. Agents cannot approve their own material output.
- Legal packages belong inside operational workflows and must link to services/engagements.
- External providers stay behind the Integration Hub.
- SkillBridge people are existing Talent Network candidates. Do not duplicate a candidate per employer.
- Scout is the official persistent assistant (tooltip: Open Scout). Commands are a closed registry. Never generate SQL. Chat is not the system of record.
